An argument that lands in a chunk position of a key — a producer, a procedure
path, a config resource or group — is a name the grammar has to be able to
spell (RFC 03 §2). The typed builders in `zenkey::selector` *assert* on an
illegal chunk, which is right for the registry constants they were written for
and wrong for a shell: `zenctl service call h-0123456789ab MyApp foo` against a
live bus panicked with **exit 101**, outside the 0/1/2 contract (#509).

Every such argument now goes through one clap `value_parser` built on
`zenkey::grammar::is_valid_plain_chunk` — the predicate the builders and the
registry linter share — so it is a usage error: exit 2, naming the argument and
the rule, before any session is opened. That is why none of these needs a bus.
The list is every verb that takes one; a new one belongs here.

```console
$ zenctl service call h-0123456789ab MyApp introspect
? 2
error: invalid value 'MyApp' for '<PRODUCER>': not a plain chunk, nor `-` for a service origin — RFC 03 §2: [a-z0-9]([a-z0-9._-]*[a-z0-9])?, lowercase, alphanumeric at both ends

For more information, try '--help'.

```

```console
$ zenctl service call h-0123456789ab probe Ping
? 2
error: invalid value 'Ping' for '<PROCEDURE>': "Ping" is not a plain chunk; a procedure path is plain chunks joined by `/` — RFC 03 §2: [a-z0-9]([a-z0-9._-]*[a-z0-9])?, lowercase, alphanumeric at both ends

For more information, try '--help'.

```

```console
$ zenctl service call h-0123456789ab probe 'artifact//status'
? 2
error: invalid value 'artifact//status' for '<PROCEDURE>': "" is not a plain chunk; a procedure path is plain chunks joined by `/` — RFC 03 §2: [a-z0-9]([a-z0-9._-]*[a-z0-9])?, lowercase, alphanumeric at both ends

For more information, try '--help'.

```

